.TH LIBTLS_TLS_NEW 3 "2023-04-01" "libtls" "TLS Library"
.SH NAME
tls_new - Create a new TLS instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libtls.h>
.sp
.B tls_t*
.B tls_new(tls_ctx_t* ctx, fd_type fd);
.B tls_t*
.B tls_client(fd_type fd);
.B tls_t*
.B tls_server(fd_type fd);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B tls_new
function creates a new TLS instance.
The function takes a
.IR ctx " "
and a
.IR fd " "
as arguments.
The function returns a pointer to the new TLS instance.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B tls_new
function to create a new TLS instance:
.nf
.B #include <libtls.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.sp
.B int main() {
.B   tls_t* tls = tls_new(tls_client_ctx, fd);
.B   if(tls == NULL) {
.B     // Handle error
.B   }
.B   // Use tls
.B   return 0;
.B }
.ne
.fi
